---
import "../styles/custom.css"
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro"
import SiteNav from "../components/SiteNav.astro"
const title = 'Pricing — Vectis Mail'
const description = 'Vectis Mail pricing — free Starter tier (3 domains, 25 mailboxes), Pro at $39 USD per tenant/month with unlimited domains and OIDC SSO, and Enterprise from $499 USD/month with SAML 2.0 SSO, a support SLA, and GDPR compliance tooling (DSAR export & data retention).'
---
<html lang="en">
<head>
	<meta charset="utf-8" />
	<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
	<title>{title}</title>
	<meta name="description" content={description} />
	<meta property="og:title" content={title} />
	<meta property="og:description" content={description} />
	<meta property="og:type" content="website" />
	<meta property="og:url" content="https://vectismail.com/pricing/" />
	<meta property="og:image" content="https://vectismail.com/og/default.png" />
	<meta property="og:image:width" content="1200" />
	<meta property="og:image:height" content="630" />
	<meta property="og:image:alt" content="Vectis Mail pricing — free Starter, $39 USD/tenant/month Pro, Enterprise from $499 USD/month" />
	<meta property="og:site_name" content="Vectis Mail" />
	<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
	<meta name="twitter:title" content={title} />
	<meta name="twitter:description" content={description} />
	<meta name="twitter:image" content="https://vectismail.com/og/default.png" />
	<meta name="theme-color" content="#0C0C0D" />
	<link rel="canonical" href="https://vectismail.com/pricing/" />
	<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
	<link rel="icon" type="image/x-icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="32x32" />
	<script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
		"@context": "https://schema.org",
		"@type": "SoftwareApplication",
		"name": "Vectis Mail",
		"applicationCategory": "CommunicationApplication",
		"applicationSubCategory": "Email Server",
		"operatingSystem": "Linux",
		"description": description,
		"url": "https://vectismail.com/pricing/",
		"softwareVersion": "0.1.21",
		"publisher": {
			"@type": "Organization",
			"name": "Veltara Works",
			"url": "https://veltaraworks.com"
		},
		"offers": [
			{
				"@type": "Offer",
				"name": "Starter",
				"price": "0",
				"priceCurrency": "USD",
				"availability": "https://schema.org/InStock",
				"description": "Free forever. Up to 3 domains, 25 mailboxes per domain, sending API, inbound webhooks, admin dashboard, Roundcube webmail, DKIM/SPF/DMARC, automatic TLS, backup and restore, RBAC + TOTP MFA, atomic updates, IP warmup, RBL monitoring, Prometheus-format metrics and health alerts (Grafana + Loki dashboards optional, off by default), community support.",
				"category": "free",
				"url": "https://vectismail.com/getting-started/installation"
			},
			{
				"@type": "Offer",
				"name": "Pro",
				"price": "39",
				"priceCurrency": "USD",
				"availability": "https://schema.org/InStock",
				"description": "Per tenant per month, never per email — unlimited send volume. Everything in Starter plus unlimited domains, unlimited mailboxes per domain, per-domain analytics dashboard, per-domain spam controls (reject thresholds, greylisting, allow/block lists), OIDC SSO (Google, Azure AD, Keycloak), priority email support, and offline use through your current paid period (typically up to ~30 days on monthly plans) if ValidonX is temporarily unreachable. One subscription covers unlimited Vectis Mail installs operated by your organisation.",
				"category": "subscription",
				"priceSpecification": {
					"@type": "UnitPriceSpecification",
					"price": "39",
					"priceCurrency": "USD",
					"unitText": "per tenant per month",
					"billingIncrement": "1",
					"billingDuration": "P1M"
				},
				"url": "https://vectismail.com/upgrade/"
			},
				{
					"@type": "Offer",
					"name": "Enterprise",
					"price": "499",
					"priceCurrency": "USD",
					"availability": "https://schema.org/InStock",
					"description": "From $499 USD per tenant per month, flat — never per seat; custom pricing for larger organisations. Everything in Pro plus SAML 2.0 single sign-on, a business-hours support SLA (first-response targets), and GDPR compliance tooling (DSAR export & erasure, data-retention controls). Roadmap: deliverability monitoring, SCIM. Sold via talk-to-us.",
					"category": "subscription",
					"url": "https://vectismail.com/talk-to-us/"
				}
		]
	})} />
	<script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
		"@context": "https://schema.org",
		"@type": "FAQPage",
		"mainEntity": [
				{
					"@type": "Question",
					"name": "What does the Enterprise plan include?",
					"acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Enterprise is for organisations that need assurance, regardless of size: everything in Pro plus SAML 2.0 single sign-on, a business-hours support SLA, and GDPR compliance tooling (DSAR export & erasure, data-retention controls). It is flat-priced from $499 USD per tenant per month — never per seat — with custom pricing for larger organisations. Deliverability monitoring and SCIM are on the roadmap; tell us what you need at https://vectismail.com/talk-to-us/." }
				},
				{
					"@type": "Question",
					"name": "What does the Enterprise support SLA cover?",
					"acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "The Enterprise SLA sets first-response targets by severity during business hours (9am–5pm AEST, Mon–Fri, excluding Australian public holidays): P1 (production mail flow down) 4 business hours, P2 (major feature degraded) 8 business hours, P3 (minor) 2 business days, P4 (question) 3 business days. These are first-response targets, not resolution times, and cover the Vectis Mail software — not customer infrastructure, DNS or deliverability, third-party components, or modified/unsupported versions. 24/7 priority response is available as a custom add-on. Because Vectis Mail is self-hosted, we do not offer an uptime SLA — your server’s availability is yours to run." }
				},
			{
				"@type": "Question",
				"name": "Why is Pro priced per tenant and not per email?",
				"acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Because metered sending punishes growth. SendGrid, Postmark, Resend, and SES all price per email past a base bucket, so your email bill rises with your send volume. Vectis Mail never charges per email — Pro is a flat $39 USD per tenant per month for unlimited send volume, whether you send 10,000 or 10 million. A tenant is your organisation, and one subscription covers unlimited Vectis Mail installs you operate." }
			},
			{
				"@type": "Question",
				"name": "Do I need a license to use Vectis Mail?",
				"acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "The Starter tier is free forever with no license required. Pro is licensed and billed through ValidonX, the default licensing backend operated by Veltara Works — though the endpoint Pro checks is a configurable URL, not a hardwired dependency." }
			},
			{
				"@type": "Question",
				"name": "What happens if my license expires?",
				"acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Your mail server keeps running and all core mail delivery continues. If a payment fails, Pro features keep working through a 21-day grace window while we retry; after that they revert to Starter limits, but your data is never locked." }
			},
			{
				"@type": "Question",
				"name": "Can I self-host without any external dependencies?",
				"acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes, and your mail is never coupled to a licensing service. Starter runs fully offline with no licensing backend. For Pro, the licensing backend is a configurable endpoint (ValidonX is the default, not a hardwired dependency); it exchanges only an opaque tenant identifier and entitlement flags — no mailboxes, message content, or recipient addresses. Core mail delivery never depends on it, and entitlements are cached in your Postgres so Pro keeps working offline through your current paid period if the backend is unreachable." }
			},
			{
				"@type": "Question",
				"name": "Am I locked into ValidonX?",
				"acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "No. The licensing backend is a URL you set, and Pro entitlement checks speak a documented HTTP contract, so the licensing layer is not hardwired to one provider. ValidonX is the default and what Pro is billed through. Combined with the source-available BSL 1.1 licence (which converts to Apache 2.0 four years after each release), there is no lock-in: your data lives in your Postgres, your mail runs on your server, and you can read, audit, or fork the code." }
			},
			{
				"@type": "Question",
				"name": "What server do I need?",
				"acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Minimum: 2 vCPU, 4 GB RAM, 40 GB SSD, Ubuntu 22.04+. Recommended for production: 4 vCPU, 8 GB RAM, 100 GB SSD. Any VPS provider works." }
			},
			{
				"@type": "Question",
				"name": "Can I resell Vectis Mail as a hosted service?",
				"acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "No. Vectis Mail is licensed under the Business Source License 1.1. You may run it for your own organisation and your own end users, including operating mail for customers of your organisation — but you may not offer Vectis Mail itself to third parties on a hosted, embedded, or managed-service basis in a way that competes with Veltara Works's paid version(s). For resale or hosted-platform licensing, contact licensing@veltaraworks.com." }
			},
			{
				"@type": "Question",
				"name": "When does Vectis Mail become Apache 2.0?",
				"acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Each version of Vectis Mail converts to Apache License 2.0 four years after that version's first public release — not a single repo-wide flip. For example, v0.1.0-beta1 (released 2026-04-25) converts on 2030-04-25; v0.1.12 (released 2026-05-10) converts on 2030-05-10. Source is available throughout, and once a version reaches its Change Date, anyone can fork, host, or relicense that specific version under Apache 2.0." }
			}
		]
	})} />
</head>
<body class="marketing-page">
	<SiteNav />

	<main>

	<section class="section" style="text-align: center;">
		<h1>Vectis Mail&trade; pricing</h1>
		<p class="subtitle">Self-hosted email — never priced per send. Free Starter tier, $39 USD/tenant/month Pro for unlimited volume. Start free, upgrade when you need more.</p>

		<div class="pricing-grid" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 240px), 360px)); justify-content: center;">
			<div class="pricing-card">
				<div class="tier">Starter</div>
				<div class="price">Free</div>
				<div class="period">forever</div>
				<ul>
					<li>Up to 3 domains</li>
					<li>Up to 25 mailboxes per domain</li>
					<li>Admin dashboard</li>
					<li>Webmail (Roundcube)</li>
					<li>Sending API + batch sending</li>
					<li>Inbound webhooks (full body)</li>
					<li>Sieve filter management</li>
					<li>DKIM/SPF/DMARC</li>
					<li>Automatic TLS</li>
					<li>Built-in metrics &amp; health alerts (Grafana + Loki optional)</li>
					<li>IP warmup &amp; RBL monitoring</li>
					<li>Backup &amp; restore</li>
					<li>Community support</li>
				</ul>
				<a href="/getting-started/installation/" class="btn-primary" style="display: block; text-align: center;">Get Started</a>
			</div>

			<div class="pricing-card featured">
				<div class="tier">Pro</div>
				<div class="price">$39</div>
				<div class="period">USD per tenant / month</div>
				<ul>
					<li>One subscription, unlimited Vectis installs</li>
					<li>Everything in Starter, plus:</li>
					<li>Unlimited send volume &mdash; never priced per email</li>
					<li>Unlimited domains</li>
					<li>Unlimited mailboxes per domain</li>
					<li>Per-domain analytics dashboard</li>
					<li>Per-domain spam controls &mdash; thresholds, greylisting, allow/block lists</li>
					<li>OIDC SSO</li>
					<li>Priority email support</li>
				</ul>
				<a href="/upgrade/" class="btn-primary" style="display: block; text-align: center;">Buy Pro — $39 USD/mo</a>
				<p style="margin-top: 1rem; font-size: 0.85rem; line-height: 1.5; opacity: 0.85;">At high volume the gap widens: SendGrid Pro starts at <strong>$89.95/mo</strong> (a dedicated IP is included; additional IPs are $30/mo each), and Resend Scale runs from <strong>$90 to $1,150/mo</strong> by send volume. Vectis Pro is <strong>$39 flat</strong> &mdash; the same price whether you send 10,000 or 10 million. <span style="opacity: 0.75;">Competitor pricing retrieved 14 Jun 2026 from <a href="https://sendgrid.com/en-us/pricing" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">SendGrid</a> and <a href="https://resend.com/pricing" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">Resend</a>.</span></p>
			</div>
				<div class="pricing-card">
					<div class="tier">Enterprise</div>
					<div class="price">From $499</div>
					<div class="period">USD per tenant / month · custom above</div>
					<ul>
						<li>Everything in Pro, plus:</li>
						<li>SAML 2.0 SSO</li>
						<li>GDPR compliance tooling &mdash; DSAR export &amp; erasure, data-retention controls</li>
						<li>Support SLA &mdash; business-hours response targets</li>
						<li>Critical security-patch commitments</li>
						<li>Flat pricing &mdash; never per seat</li>
						<li style="opacity: 0.7;">Roadmap: deliverability monitoring, SCIM</li>
					</ul>
					<a href="/talk-to-us/" class="btn-primary" style="display: block; text-align: center;">Talk to us</a>
					<p style="margin-top: 1rem; font-size: 0.85rem; line-height: 1.5; opacity: 0.85;">For organisations that need SAML, an SLA, or compliance tooling. Flat per-tenant pricing &mdash; where Microsoft 365 and Google Workspace bill per seat, Enterprise stays flat as you grow.</p>
				</div>

		</div>

		<p class="subtitle" style="margin-top: 2rem; font-size: 0.95rem;">
			Running mail for client domains? Agency plans are in the works &mdash; <a href="/talk-to-us/">tell us what you need</a> and we’ll size it with you. Need a larger or custom Enterprise plan? <a href="/talk-to-us/">Talk to us</a>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<h2>Starter vs Pro vs Enterprise at a glance</h2>
		<div class="compare-table-wrap" style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
			<table class="compare-table">
						<thead>
							<tr>
								<th scope="col">Feature</th>
								<th scope="col">Starter</th>
								<th scope="col">Pro</th>
								<th scope="col">Enterprise</th>
							</tr>
						</thead>
						<tbody>
							<tr><td>Price</td><td>Free forever</td><td>$39 USD / tenant / month</td><td>From $499 USD / tenant / month</td></tr>
							<tr><td>Domains</td><td>Up to 3</td><td>Unlimited</td><td>Unlimited</td></tr>
							<tr><td>Mailboxes per domain</td><td>Up to 25</td><td>Unlimited</td><td>Unlimited</td></tr>
							<tr><td>Sending API + batch sending</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
							<tr><td>Inbound webhooks (full body)</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
							<tr><td>Admin dashboard</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
							<tr><td>Webmail (Roundcube)</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
							<tr><td>Sieve filter management</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
							<tr><td>DKIM / SPF / DMARC</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
							<tr><td>Automatic TLS</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
							<tr><td>Monitoring (metrics + health alerts; Grafana + Loki optional)</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
							<tr><td>IP warmup &amp; RBL monitoring</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
							<tr><td>Backup &amp; restore</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
							<tr><td>Per-domain analytics dashboard</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
							<tr><td>Per-domain spam controls (thresholds, greylisting, allow/block)</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
							<tr><td>OIDC SSO (Google, Azure AD, Keycloak)</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
							<tr><td>SAML 2.0 SSO</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
							<tr><td>Support</td><td>Community</td><td>Priority email</td><td>Priority email + SLA</td></tr>
							<tr><td>Support SLA (first-response targets)</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
							<tr><td>Critical security-patch commitment</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
							<tr><td>GDPR DSAR export &amp; erasure</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
							<tr><td>Data-retention controls (PII purge)</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
							<tr><td>Advanced deliverability monitoring</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>Roadmap</td></tr>
							<tr><td>SCIM provisioning</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>Roadmap</td></tr>
							<tr><td>Offline use if ValidonX is unreachable</td><td>n/a</td><td>Through current paid period</td><td>Through current paid period</td></tr>
						</tbody>
					</table>
		</div>
	</section>

		<section class="section">
			<h2>Enterprise assurance</h2>
			<p class="subtitle" style="margin-top: 0.5rem;">For organisations that need SAML, a support SLA, and compliance tooling — regardless of size. Flat per-tenant pricing from $499 USD/month, never per seat, custom above.</p>
			<h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">Support SLA — first-response targets</h3>
			<div class="compare-table-wrap" style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">
				<table class="compare-table">
					<thead>
						<tr><th scope="col">Severity</th><th scope="col">Example</th><th scope="col">First response</th></tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr><td>P1 &mdash; Critical</td><td>Production mail flow down, no workaround</td><td>4 business hours</td></tr>
						<tr><td>P2 &mdash; High</td><td>Major feature degraded</td><td>8 business hours</td></tr>
						<tr><td>P3 &mdash; Normal</td><td>Minor issue, workaround exists</td><td>2 business days</td></tr>
						<tr><td>P4 &mdash; Low</td><td>Question or cosmetic</td><td>3 business days</td></tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
			<p style="margin-top: 1rem; font-size: 0.9rem; opacity: 0.85;">Business hours are 9am&ndash;5pm AEST, Monday&ndash;Friday, excluding Australian public holidays. These are <strong>first-response targets, not resolution times</strong>. Coverage is for the Vectis Mail software and excludes customer infrastructure, networks, DNS and deliverability, third-party components, and modified or unsupported versions. 24/7 priority response is available as a custom add-on &mdash; <a href="/talk-to-us/">talk to us</a>. We also commit to issuing critical security patches promptly and prioritising confirmed critical fixes into the next patch release.</p>
			<h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">Deliverability, honestly</h3>
			<p style="font-size: 0.9rem; opacity: 0.85;">Vectis Mail is self-hosted, so inbox placement ultimately rides on your own server&rsquo;s IP reputation — which we equip and advise on, but do not own. We don&rsquo;t sell &ldquo;guaranteed deliverability&rdquo;. What we provide: correct DKIM/SPF/DMARC out of the box, the dual-send warmup migration playbook (keep your current provider live while your new IP warms), and RBL monitoring today — with reputation/blocklist alerting on the Enterprise roadmap. For the same reason, we do not offer an uptime SLA: your server&rsquo;s availability is yours to run.</p>
			<p style="margin-top: 1.25rem;"><a href="/talk-to-us/" class="btn-primary" style="display:inline-block;">Talk to us about Enterprise</a></p>
		</section>

	<section class="section">
		<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
		<div class="feature-grid" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 400px), 1fr));">
			<div class="feature-card">
				<h3>Why per tenant and not per email?</h3>
				<p>Because metered sending punishes growth. SendGrid, Postmark, Resend, and SES all price per email past a base bucket, so your bill rises with your send volume. Vectis Mail <strong>never charges per email</strong> — Pro is a flat $39 USD per tenant per month for unlimited volume, the same price whether you send 10,000 or 10 million. A tenant is your organisation, and one subscription covers unlimited Vectis Mail installs you operate.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="feature-card">
				<h3>Do I need a license to use Vectis Mail?</h3>
				<p>The Starter tier is free forever with no license required. Pro is licensed and billed through <a href="https://validonx.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">ValidonX</a>, the default licensing backend (operated by Veltara Works) — though the endpoint Pro checks is configurable, not a hardwired dependency.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="feature-card">
				<h3>What happens if my Pro license expires?</h3>
				<p>Your mail server keeps running and all core mail delivery (Postfix, Dovecot) continues working. If a payment fails, Pro features keep working through a 21-day grace window while we retry; after that, Pro features (analytics, advanced spam controls, OIDC SSO, unlimited domains and mailboxes) revert to Starter limits but your data is never locked.</p>
			</div>
				<div class="feature-card">
					<h3>What does the Enterprise plan include?</h3>
					<p>Enterprise is for organisations that need <strong>assurance</strong>, regardless of size: everything in Pro plus <strong>SAML 2.0 SSO</strong>, a <strong>business-hours support SLA</strong>, and <strong>GDPR compliance tooling</strong> (DSAR export &amp; erasure, data-retention controls). It&rsquo;s flat-priced <strong>from $499 USD per tenant per month</strong> &mdash; never per seat &mdash; with custom pricing for larger organisations. Deliverability monitoring and SCIM are on the roadmap. <a href="/talk-to-us/" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">Tell us what you need</a> and we&rsquo;ll size it with you.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="feature-card">
					<h3>What does the Enterprise support SLA cover?</h3>
					<p>First-response targets by severity during business hours (9am&ndash;5pm AEST, Mon&ndash;Fri, excl. AU public holidays): <strong>P1 4 business hours</strong>, P2 8 business hours, P3 2 business days, P4 3 business days. These are first-response targets, not resolution times, and cover the Vectis Mail software &mdash; not your infrastructure, DNS/deliverability, third-party components, or modified versions. 24/7 priority response is a custom add-on. Because Vectis Mail is self-hosted, we don&rsquo;t offer an uptime SLA &mdash; your server&rsquo;s availability is yours to run.</p>
				</div>
			<div class="feature-card">
				<h3>Can I self-host without any external dependencies?</h3>
				<p>Yes — and your mail is never coupled to a licensing service. Starter runs fully offline with no licensing backend at all. For Pro, the licensing backend is a <strong>configurable endpoint</strong> (<a href="https://validonx.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">ValidonX</a> is the default we operate, not a hardwired dependency): it exchanges only an opaque tenant identifier and your entitlement flags — no mailboxes, message content, or recipient addresses ever pass through it. Core mail delivery (Postfix, Dovecot) never depends on it, and Pro entitlements are cached in your Postgres so they keep working offline through your current paid period if the backend is unreachable.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="feature-card">
				<h3>Am I locked into ValidonX?</h3>
				<p>No. The licensing backend is a URL you set, and Pro entitlement checks speak a documented HTTP contract — so the licensing layer isn't hardwired to one provider. ValidonX (operated by Veltara Works) is the default and what Pro is billed through; it's a convenience, not a chain. Combined with the source-available <a href="https://github.com/Veltara-Works/vectis/blob/main/LICENSE" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">BSL 1.1</a> licence (which converts to Apache 2.0 four years after each release), there's no lock-in: your data lives in your Postgres, your mail runs on your server, and you can read, audit, or fork the code.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="feature-card">
				<h3>What server do I need?</h3>
				<p>Minimum: 2 vCPU, 4 GB RAM, 40 GB SSD, Ubuntu 22.04+. Recommended for production: 4 vCPU, 8 GB RAM, 100 GB SSD. Any VPS provider works.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="feature-card">
				<h3>Can I resell Vectis Mail as a hosted service?</h3>
